One playthrough and I'm stunned!
- Best storyline I've seen in a while;
- Surprisingly rich replayability;
- Tough moral choices combined with economical and political "tycoon-type" simulation;
- Decent graphics;
- Decent controls;
- Would give the soundtrack some improvement but it IS GOOD!
Probably my choice for Indie Game of the Year. I'm very grateful to the developers and look forward towards a new playthrough and new endings!

(KEEP IN MIND THIS GAME IS STILL IN PRE-ALPHA STAGE)
Patch 0.6.0.
Some players argue that the game is too much expensive (31,99€), but please remember that this money will be used to help in the development of the game. EmergeNYC has the potencial to be a very, VERY good and fun game. Don't feel afraid with the "Early Access" warning. I am 100% confident that the team working on the game is not going to give up on it. Update after update, you can feel the love, dedication and efforts of the devs to make EmergeNYC the best experience you can have in this type of game. FlipSwitch has raised $44,000 USD by 853 backers on Indiegogo and $13,081 USD by 198 backers on Kickstarter. There is also a discussion on Steam, a Discord server and an official website where you can report any bugs and/or give sugestions to improve the game, and the devs ACTUALLY listen to every word in there and take every comment in mind when working on the game.
The Promises:
It has been promised in the full version of the game the ability for players to being able to be part of the FDNY, FDNY EMS and NYPD, aswell as being able to use every member of a squad, each of them with unique equipment depending on the department you are working. There is also going to be fires, car crashes, shootings, pre-hospital care and even prank calls! The multiplayer servers will have a maximum of 32 players in the same server. Every call will require the use of IRL skills used by the emergency services and the knowledge of the use of every tool avaiable.
Patch and review (0.6.0)
City of New York is 100% complete with all the buildings and subways. NY has been temporary disabled due to multiplayer issues. Multiplayer has been temporary disabled for bug fixing.

Fire Academy, 5 new buildings where you can spawn different types of emergencies and train the correct procedures.
Usable items, such as hoses, K-12 saws, the halligan tool and fire extinguishers.
Firefighting mechanics and breaching mechanics. You can now put out fire, use saws to cut locks and use ladders to get to rooftops.
First and third person gameplay with individual firefighters and smoother enter/exit vehicle.
Health and oxygen bars.
SCBA on/off. Also has influence on the oxygen.
Pros:
- Gorgeous firetrucks models;
- Good ambulances and police cars models;
- Customizable police cars, lightbars, colors, etc;
- Realistic driving;
- Awesome sirens, where you can choose between 3 automatic horns + 1 airhorn + 1 or 2 manual horns (depending on the truck);
- Awesome emergency lights;
- Third and first person views avaiable;
- Fire Academy, where you can give wings to your imagination;
- More freedom (comparing to previous versions).
Cons:
- Traffic is still a mess;
- Traffic lights don't fully work at the moment;
- Multiplayer full of bugs;
- Game poorly optimised (if you have a low-end PC, you will have a bad time trying to run the game);
- Bad looking and bugged firefighter models;
- NYC and Multiplayer disabled.

Overall review:
The game has a lot of potencial and I fully recommend to invest your money and your time in this game. You will find the demo very entertaining just by exploring everything it is offered to you and the feeling you get everytime there is an update waiting for you to be downloaded with new and fresh content.

